+All methods in this family project 3D geometry onto 2D planes and aggregate the resulting fragments into a 3D voxel grid [G]. The common mechanism consists of the following steps:
 1. **Camera Configuration:** Orthographic cameras are positioned along specific axes (e.g., X, Y, Z) looking towards the scene's axis-aligned bounding box (AABB) [G].
